{
  "id": "v29-runs-file-header",
  "asserts": "`runs` lists a TypeScript container by the TEST FILE it ran, not by its argv: every worker of one vitest invocation has the same thirty-character `node .../workers/forks.js` command line, and a listing of them is unreadable. `meta.test_file` is the root-relative path of the one file this container ran, and its ABSENCE is a statement rather than a gap -- a container that ran several files carries `test_files` and prints `files: N`, one that ran none (a `globalSetup`, any `node --test` process) carries neither and keeps the argv (`typescript/HONESTY.md` §6). One vector describes one trace, so the `test_files` arm is held by `tests/test_vocab.py::test_a_reused_worker_is_listed_by_its_file_count`, built with this same builder and run through the same real CLI.",
